      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: If a file or category is present in the `before` traces but completely removed in the `after` traces (or newly added), it will be missing from `a_map` (or `b_map`). This fallback creates a `Stat` with `n\u003d1` (`Stat([0.0])`). If `has_multi_run` is True, `compute_p_value` will return `None` because `n \u003c 2`, and this item will be silently excluded from the statistical test and the final report instead of being flagged as a major change.\n\nConsider passing `b_run_count` and `a_run_count` to this function and using `Stat([0.0] * b_run_count)` and `Stat([0.0] * a_run_count)` respectively so these items correctly participate in the p-value calculation.",
